{{define "title"}}Someone tried to sign up with your email address{{end}}
{{define "content"}}
{{/*
  Nothing in this message may describe the account beyond the single fact that
  it exists. No handle, no creation date, no account state, no second-factor
  status. Whoever typed the address is unauthenticated, so nothing about THEM
  appears either — no address, no location, no device — and the event this
  renders from deliberately carries none of it (ADR-055, ADR-002).
*/}}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">Hello{{if .Name}} {{.Name}}{{end}},</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">On <strong>{{datetime .OccurredAt}}</strong>, somebody tried to create a Chronos
  account with this email address. No new account was created: this address already has one.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">If that was you, you do not need to sign up again — sign in instead.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">
  <a href="{{url "/sign-in"}}" style="display:inline-block;background:#1a1d21;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;padding:11px 20px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;">Sign in</a>
</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">Forgotten your password? <a href="{{url "/forgot-password"}}" style="color:#3b5bdb;">Set a new one</a>.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">If it was not you, you can ignore this message. Nothing changed: no account was
  created, your password was not altered, and nobody was told anything about your account. Whoever typed
  your address saw exactly what they would have seen if this address had no account at all.</p>
<p style="margin:0;color:#6b7280;font-size:13px;">We send this at most a few times an hour for one address,
  so repeated attempts will not fill your inbox.</p>
{{end}}
